REVISE

REASONS
1. [a] The contract-level policy is correct in principle: `resolve_mounted_skills`/`is_skill_mountable` now gate by `contract.skills` and default `base_skills=()` is empty.  
2. [b] Default-empty + union is the right “host escape hatch” posture (no implicit broadening).  
3. [c] The additive `BuildContract.skills: tuple[str, ...] = ()` is sound for a frozen, serializable model and keeps existing behavior unchanged by default.  
4. [d] Test coverage validates the helper semantics, but it does not yet prove end-to-end enforcement in the actual Build/Agent mount pipeline, and does not lock down “all other built-ins default-empty” invariants centrally.

REQUIRED_REVISIONS
1. Wire `resolve_mounted_skills`/`is_skill_mountable` into the actual skill-MCP mount path used at run/build setup (if not already done elsewhere) so this is enforced, not just unit-tested.
2. Add an integration test for the mount path that uses real available skills plus an undeclared contract and verifies the undeclared skill is not mounted.
3. Add a contract-registry-level regression test asserting all non-appkit builtins have empty `skills` unless explicitly declared.
